  "question": {
    "text": "A balloon is rising vertically upwards. At an instant, an observer on the ground, whose distance from the balloon is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math>&nbsp;meters, sees the balloon at an angle of elevation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>30</mn><mtext>o</mtext></msup><mo>.</mo></math> If the balloon rises further vertically to a point where the angle of elevation as seen by the observer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>45</mn><mtext>o</mtext></msup></math>, then its height (in meters) from the ground is<br />\r(Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1.</mn><mn>73</mn></math>)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "36.5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0023_093608c09ee6.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 191px;\" /><br />Let <math><mi>A</mi></math> be the observer,&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi></math> be the initial position of the balloon and it is at <math><mi>Q</mi></math> when the angle of elevation is <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mn>45</mn></mrow> <mtext>o</mtext> </msup> </mrow> </math></p><p>From triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;and triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>Q</mi></math><br />and&nbsp;<math><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math><br />So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>73</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;meters</p>"
  }
}